    "note": "Two sheets of one character with one framing. Each frame of both has a `waist` socket (untrimmed-frame pixels; flipX: x = frameWidth - x). Draw the legs frame for the walk direction at the character's ground point (the usual pivot), then the torso frame for the aim direction on top, placed so its waist socket lands on the legs frame's waist socket: torso.x = legs.x + legsWaist.x - torsoWaist.x (same for y), in untrimmed-frame pixels. The torso always draws over the legs. A clip on both sheets (idle, crouch, death\u2026) drawn in one direction is the whole body again."
